---
title: Provisioning (Advanced)
id: provisioning
order: 5
description: "Give the in-sandbox agent secrets, skill repos, MCP servers, plugins, and instructions with one portable definition that each harness projects into its own native format."
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provisioning is how you hand the in-sandbox agent everything beyond the working\ntree: typed secrets, skill repos, MCP servers, plugins, and a universal\ninstruction file. You declare it all on "},{"type":"link","href":"./workspace","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineWorkspace()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and\neach harness adapter projects it into its own native format at bootstrap, so\nthe same definition works whether the agent is Grok Build, Claude Code, Codex, or OpenCode."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  bearer,\n  createSecrets,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  fileSkill,\n  gitSkill,\n  githubRepo,\n  mcpSkill,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/tanstack-skills' }),\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH }),\n    mcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n      url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n      headers: { Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY) },\n    }),\n    fileSkill({ path: '.agent-hints.md', content: '# Hints\\nPrefer pnpm.' }),\n  ],\n  plugins: ['@anthropic/plugin-foo'],\n  instructions: 'Always run `pnpm test` before proposing a change.',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-safe-secrets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type-safe secrets"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSecrets"},{"type":"text","value":" turns plain environment values into opaque "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SecretRef"},{"type":"text","value":" tokens.\nYou pass the refs around your config; the underlying strings stay out of every\nserializable surface."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  secrets,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"secrets"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"link","href":"./workspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"declared on the workspace"}]},{"type":"text","value":". At create, resume, and\nsnapshot restore, the sandbox layer resolves them onto the live handle env.\nProviders never write those values into snapshots, the sandbox store, or the\nevent log."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"why-the-values-never-leak","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why the values never leak"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The real strings are held in a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"non-enumerable, symbol-keyed registry"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on the\nobject "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSecrets"},{"type":"text","value":" returns. Each property you access ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"secrets.GH"},{"type":"text","value":") is a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SecretRef"},{"type":"text","value":" token, not the string. Because the registry is symbol-keyed and\nnon-enumerable:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.keys(secrets)"},{"type":"text","value":", spreads, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify(secrets)"},{"type":"text","value":" never expose\nthe values."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The values are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"never written to snapshots, the sandbox store, or the event\nlog"}]},{"type":"text","value":". They are resolved only when the live sandbox env is built."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is what makes the workspace definition safe to hash, persist, and replay\nfor resume bookkeeping without ever persisting a credential."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"passing-a-secret-where-a-secretref-is-accepted","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passing a secret where a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SecretRef"},{"type":"text","value":" is accepted"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hand a ref directly to any field that takes one. The clearest example is\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill"},{"type":"text","value":" auth: pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"secret: secrets.GH"},{"type":"text","value":" and the token is resolved only when\nthe repo is cloned:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, gitSkill, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({ GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '' })\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH })],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"bearer-ref-for-header-values","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bearer(ref)"},{"type":"text","value":" for header values"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In MCP header values you can use a ref directly, or wrap it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bearer(ref)"},{"type":"text","value":"\nto produce a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Bearer <value>"},{"type":"text","value":" string at resolution time:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { bearer, createSecrets, mcpSkill } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\nmcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n  url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n  headers: {\n    Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY), // resolves to \"Bearer <value>\"\n    'X-Token': secrets.GH, // resolves to the raw token value\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"skills-plugins-and-mcp-servers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skills, plugins, and MCP servers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"},{"type":"text","value":" is an array of skill values that provision capabilities into the\nagent's environment. There are four builders, each describing a different kind\nof capability:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it provisions"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"agentSkill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A named public skill (portable placeholder; Claude Code warns and skips it, so use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill"},{"type":"text","value":" instead)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A skill repo cloned into the workspace, with optional auth and clone path."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcpSkill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A third-party MCP server, with URL and headers."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileSkill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An arbitrary file written into the workspace."}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  bearer,\n  createSecrets,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  fileSkill,\n  gitSkill,\n  githubRepo,\n  mcpSkill,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    // Clone a public skill repo (preferred over agentSkill on Claude Code).\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/tanstack-skills' }),\n    // Clone a private skill repo; `secret` is resolved from the secrets registry.\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH }),\n    // Wire an MCP server with a resolved bearer token in the Authorization header.\n    mcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n      url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n      headers: { Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY) },\n    }),\n    // Write an arbitrary file into the workspace.\n    fileSkill({ path: '.agent-hints.md', content: '# Hints\\nPrefer pnpm.' }),\n  ],\n  plugins: ['@anthropic/plugin-foo'],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"gitskill-clone-path","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill"},{"type":"text","value":" clone path"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill"},{"type":"text","value":" takes an optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"into"},{"type":"text","value":" field, an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"absolute path inside the\nsandbox"}]},{"type":"text","value":", controlling where the repo is cloned. It defaults to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".tanstack-skills/<repo-basename>"},{"type":"text","value":". Bootstrap creates the parent directory\nbefore the clone."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paths that start with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/workspace"},{"type":"text","value":" use the portable workspace root. The\nprovider maps that root onto its real workdir. Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/workspace/..."},{"type":"text","value":" in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"into"},{"type":"text","value":" unless you have a reason to pin a provider-specific path."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, gitSkill, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({ GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '' })\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    gitSkill({\n      repo: 'owner/private-skills',\n      secret: secrets.GH,\n      into: '/workspace/.skills/private',\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"per-harness-projection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-harness projection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At bootstrap each harness projector maps these values into its CLI's native\nformat:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP servers projected to"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".mcp.json"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Codex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".codex/config.toml"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenCode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opencode.json"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each projector walks the cloned repo for folders that contain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":". A\nnested pack ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills/foo/SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":") is linked under the skill name "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"foo"},{"type":"text","value":". A\nflat clone with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" at the root uses the clone name. You do not write\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ln -s"},{"type":"text","value":" by hand."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A concept a given CLI lacks (for example, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"},{"type":"text","value":" on Codex) "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"emits a\nwarning and is silently skipped"}]},{"type":"text","value":" rather than throwing. The same applies to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"agentSkill"},{"type":"text","value":" on Claude Code: there is no reliable primitive to install a public\nskill by bare name, so the projector warns and skips it. Prefer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill"},{"type":"text","value":" (or a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"},{"type":"text","value":" entry) when you need that skill on Claude Code. That keeps one\nportable definition usable across harnesses: you declare everything once, and\neach agent takes the parts it understands."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These MCP servers are third-party services you point the agent at. Bridging\nyour "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"own app's host tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" into the agent (a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" server tool whose\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute()"},{"type":"text","value":" runs back on the host) is a different mechanism, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"agents-md-and-per-harness-symlinks","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":" and per-harness symlinks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"},{"type":"text","value":" is a string written to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":" at the workspace root during\nbootstrap. Harness-specific counterparts ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLAUDE.md"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GEMINI.md"},{"type":"text","value":") are\ncreated as "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"symlinks"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to it; if the sandbox process layer cannot symlink, they\nare written as copies instead. Either way the instruction content is read\nnatively by every supported CLI without extra config."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  instructions: 'Always run `pnpm test` before proposing a change.',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"},{"type":"text","value":" for guidance you want the agent to always follow. To\nconstrain what it is "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"allowed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to do, which commands and capabilities are\nallowed, asked about, or denied, reach for "},{"type":"link","href":"./policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Policy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instead."}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-safe-secrets","text":"Type-safe secrets","level":2},{"id":"why-the-values-never-leak","text":"Why the values never leak","level":3},{"id":"passing-a-secret-where-a-secretref-is-accepted","text":"Passing a secret where a SecretRef is accepted","level":3},{"id":"bearer-ref-for-header-values","text":"bearer(ref) for header values","level":3},{"id":"skills-plugins-and-mcp-servers","text":"Skills, plugins, and MCP servers","level":2},{"id":"gitskill-clone-path","text":"gitSkill clone path","level":3},{"id":"per-harness-projection","text":"Per-harness projection","level":3},{"id":"agents-md-and-per-harness-symlinks","text":"AGENTS.md and per-harness symlinks","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nProvisioning is how you hand the in-sandbox agent everything beyond the working\ntree: typed secrets, skill repos, MCP servers, plugins, and a universal\ninstruction file. You declare it all on [`defineWorkspace()`](./workspace), and\neach harness adapter projects it into its own native format at bootstrap, so\nthe same definition works whether the agent is Grok Build, Claude Code, Codex, or OpenCode.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  bearer,\n  createSecrets,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  fileSkill,\n  gitSkill,\n  githubRepo,\n  mcpSkill,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/tanstack-skills' }),\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH }),\n    mcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n      url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n      headers: { Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY) },\n    }),\n    fileSkill({ path: '.agent-hints.md', content: '# Hints\\nPrefer pnpm.' }),\n  ],\n  plugins: ['@anthropic/plugin-foo'],\n  instructions: 'Always run `pnpm test` before proposing a change.',\n})\n```\n\n## Type-safe secrets\n\n`createSecrets` turns plain environment values into opaque `SecretRef` tokens.\nYou pass the refs around your config; the underlying strings stay out of every\nserializable surface.\n\n```ts\nimport { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  secrets,\n})\n```\n\n`secrets` is [declared on the workspace](./workspace). At create, resume, and\nsnapshot restore, the sandbox layer resolves them onto the live handle env.\nProviders never write those values into snapshots, the sandbox store, or the\nevent log.\n\n### Why the values never leak\n\nThe real strings are held in a **non-enumerable, symbol-keyed registry** on the\nobject `createSecrets` returns. Each property you access (`secrets.GH`) is a\n`SecretRef` token, not the string. Because the registry is symbol-keyed and\nnon-enumerable:\n\n- `Object.keys(secrets)`, spreads, and `JSON.stringify(secrets)` never expose\n  the values.\n- The values are **never written to snapshots, the sandbox store, or the event\n  log**. They are resolved only when the live sandbox env is built.\n\nThis is what makes the workspace definition safe to hash, persist, and replay\nfor resume bookkeeping without ever persisting a credential.\n\n### Passing a secret where a `SecretRef` is accepted\n\nHand a ref directly to any field that takes one. The clearest example is\n`gitSkill` auth: pass `secret: secrets.GH` and the token is resolved only when\nthe repo is cloned:\n\n```ts\nimport { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, gitSkill, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({ GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '' })\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH })],\n})\n```\n\n### `bearer(ref)` for header values\n\nIn MCP header values you can use a ref directly, or wrap it with `bearer(ref)`\nto produce a `Bearer <value>` string at resolution time:\n\n```ts\nimport { bearer, createSecrets, mcpSkill } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\nmcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n  url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n  headers: {\n    Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY), // resolves to \"Bearer <value>\"\n    'X-Token': secrets.GH, // resolves to the raw token value\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Skills, plugins, and MCP servers\n\n`skills` is an array of skill values that provision capabilities into the\nagent's environment. There are four builders, each describing a different kind\nof capability:\n\n| Builder      | What it provisions                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `agentSkill` | A named public skill (portable placeholder; Claude Code warns and skips it, so use `gitSkill` instead). |\n| `gitSkill`   | A skill repo cloned into the workspace, with optional auth and clone path.         |\n| `mcpSkill`   | A third-party MCP server, with URL and headers.                                    |\n| `fileSkill`  | An arbitrary file written into the workspace.                                      |\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  bearer,\n  createSecrets,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  fileSkill,\n  gitSkill,\n  githubRepo,\n  mcpSkill,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    // Clone a public skill repo (preferred over agentSkill on Claude Code).\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/tanstack-skills' }),\n    // Clone a private skill repo; `secret` is resolved from the secrets registry.\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH }),\n    // Wire an MCP server with a resolved bearer token in the Authorization header.\n    mcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n      url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n      headers: { Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY) },\n    }),\n    // Write an arbitrary file into the workspace.\n    fileSkill({ path: '.agent-hints.md', content: '# Hints\\nPrefer pnpm.' }),\n  ],\n  plugins: ['@anthropic/plugin-foo'],\n})\n```\n\n### `gitSkill` clone path\n\n`gitSkill` takes an optional `into` field, an **absolute path inside the\nsandbox**, controlling where the repo is cloned. It defaults to\n`.tanstack-skills/<repo-basename>`. Bootstrap creates the parent directory\nbefore the clone.\n\nPaths that start with `/workspace` use the portable workspace root. The\nprovider maps that root onto its real workdir. Keep `/workspace/...` in\n`into` unless you have a reason to pin a provider-specific path.\n\n```ts\nimport { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, gitSkill, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({ GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '' })\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    gitSkill({\n      repo: 'owner/private-skills',\n      secret: secrets.GH,\n      into: '/workspace/.skills/private',\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n### Per-harness projection\n\nAt bootstrap each harness projector maps these values into its CLI's native\nformat:\n\n| Harness     | MCP servers projected to |\n| ----------- | ------------------------ |\n| Claude Code | `.mcp.json`              |\n| Codex       | `.codex/config.toml`     |\n| OpenCode    | `opencode.json`          |\n\nEach projector walks the cloned repo for folders that contain `SKILL.md`. A\nnested pack (`skills/foo/SKILL.md`) is linked under the skill name `foo`. A\nflat clone with `SKILL.md` at the root uses the clone name. You do not write\n`ln -s` by hand.\n\nA concept a given CLI lacks (for example, `plugins` on Codex) **emits a\nwarning and is silently skipped** rather than throwing. The same applies to\n`agentSkill` on Claude Code: there is no reliable primitive to install a public\nskill by bare name, so the projector warns and skips it. Prefer `gitSkill` (or a\n`plugins` entry) when you need that skill on Claude Code. That keeps one\nportable definition usable across harnesses: you declare everything once, and\neach agent takes the parts it understands.\n\n> These MCP servers are third-party services you point the agent at. Bridging\n> your **own app's host tools** into the agent (a `chat()` server tool whose\n> `execute()` runs back on the host) is a different mechanism, see\n> [Tools](./tools).\n\n## `AGENTS.md` and per-harness symlinks\n\n`instructions` is a string written to `AGENTS.md` at the workspace root during\nbootstrap. Harness-specific counterparts (`CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`) are\ncreated as **symlinks** to it; if the sandbox process layer cannot symlink, they\nare written as copies instead. Either way the instruction content is read\nnatively by every supported CLI without extra config.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  instructions: 'Always run `pnpm test` before proposing a change.',\n})\n```\n\n> Use `instructions` for guidance you want the agent to always follow. To\n> constrain what it is *allowed* to do, which commands and capabilities are\n> allowed, asked about, or denied, reach for [Policy](./policy) instead.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Provisioning (Advanced)\nid: provisioning\norder: 5\ndescription: \"Give the in-sandbox agent secrets, skill repos, MCP servers, plugins, and instructions with one portable definition that each harness projects into its own native format.\"\n---\n\nProvisioning is how you hand the in-sandbox agent everything beyond the working\ntree: typed secrets, skill repos, MCP servers, plugins, and a universal\ninstruction file. You declare it all on [`defineWorkspace()`](./workspace), and\neach harness adapter projects it into its own native format at bootstrap, so\nthe same definition works whether the agent is Grok Build, Claude Code, Codex, or OpenCode.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  bearer,\n  createSecrets,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  fileSkill,\n  gitSkill,\n  githubRepo,\n  mcpSkill,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/tanstack-skills' }),\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH }),\n    mcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n      url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n      headers: { Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY) },\n    }),\n    fileSkill({ path: '.agent-hints.md', content: '# Hints\\nPrefer pnpm.' }),\n  ],\n  plugins: ['@anthropic/plugin-foo'],\n  instructions: 'Always run `pnpm test` before proposing a change.',\n})\n```\n\n## Type-safe secrets\n\n`createSecrets` turns plain environment values into opaque `SecretRef` tokens.\nYou pass the refs around your config; the underlying strings stay out of every\nserializable surface.\n\n```ts\nimport { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  secrets,\n})\n```\n\n`secrets` is [declared on the workspace](./workspace). At create, resume, and\nsnapshot restore, the sandbox layer resolves them onto the live handle env.\nProviders never write those values into snapshots, the sandbox store, or the\nevent log.\n\n### Why the values never leak\n\nThe real strings are held in a **non-enumerable, symbol-keyed registry** on the\nobject `createSecrets` returns. Each property you access (`secrets.GH`) is a\n`SecretRef` token, not the string. Because the registry is symbol-keyed and\nnon-enumerable:\n\n- `Object.keys(secrets)`, spreads, and `JSON.stringify(secrets)` never expose\n  the values.\n- The values are **never written to snapshots, the sandbox store, or the event\n  log**. They are resolved only when the live sandbox env is built.\n\nThis is what makes the workspace definition safe to hash, persist, and replay\nfor resume bookkeeping without ever persisting a credential.\n\n### Passing a secret where a `SecretRef` is accepted\n\nHand a ref directly to any field that takes one. The clearest example is\n`gitSkill` auth: pass `secret: secrets.GH` and the token is resolved only when\nthe repo is cloned:\n\n```ts\nimport { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, gitSkill, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({ GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '' })\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH })],\n})\n```\n\n### `bearer(ref)` for header values\n\nIn MCP header values you can use a ref directly, or wrap it with `bearer(ref)`\nto produce a `Bearer <value>` string at resolution time:\n\n```ts\nimport { bearer, createSecrets, mcpSkill } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\nmcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n  url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n  headers: {\n    Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY), // resolves to \"Bearer <value>\"\n    'X-Token': secrets.GH, // resolves to the raw token value\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Skills, plugins, and MCP servers\n\n`skills` is an array of skill values that provision capabilities into the\nagent's environment. There are four builders, each describing a different kind\nof capability:\n\n| Builder      | What it provisions                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `agentSkill` | A named public skill (portable placeholder; Claude Code warns and skips it, so use `gitSkill` instead). |\n| `gitSkill`   | A skill repo cloned into the workspace, with optional auth and clone path.         |\n| `mcpSkill`   | A third-party MCP server, with URL and headers.                                    |\n| `fileSkill`  | An arbitrary file written into the workspace.                                      |\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  bearer,\n  createSecrets,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  fileSkill,\n  gitSkill,\n  githubRepo,\n  mcpSkill,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({\n  GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '',\n  SENTRY: process.env.SENTRY_TOKEN ?? '',\n})\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    // Clone a public skill repo (preferred over agentSkill on Claude Code).\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/tanstack-skills' }),\n    // Clone a private skill repo; `secret` is resolved from the secrets registry.\n    gitSkill({ repo: 'owner/private-skills', secret: secrets.GH }),\n    // Wire an MCP server with a resolved bearer token in the Authorization header.\n    mcpSkill('my-mcp', {\n      url: 'https://mcp.example.com',\n      headers: { Authorization: bearer(secrets.SENTRY) },\n    }),\n    // Write an arbitrary file into the workspace.\n    fileSkill({ path: '.agent-hints.md', content: '# Hints\\nPrefer pnpm.' }),\n  ],\n  plugins: ['@anthropic/plugin-foo'],\n})\n```\n\n### `gitSkill` clone path\n\n`gitSkill` takes an optional `into` field, an **absolute path inside the\nsandbox**, controlling where the repo is cloned. It defaults to\n`.tanstack-skills/<repo-basename>`. Bootstrap creates the parent directory\nbefore the clone.\n\nPaths that start with `/workspace` use the portable workspace root. The\nprovider maps that root onto its real workdir. Keep `/workspace/...` in\n`into` unless you have a reason to pin a provider-specific path.\n\n```ts\nimport { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, gitSkill, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst secrets = createSecrets({ GH: process.env.GH_TOKEN ?? '' })\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  secrets,\n  skills: [\n    gitSkill({\n      repo: 'owner/private-skills',\n      secret: secrets.GH,\n      into: '/workspace/.skills/private',\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n### Per-harness projection\n\nAt bootstrap each harness projector maps these values into its CLI's native\nformat:\n\n| Harness     | MCP servers projected to |\n| ----------- | ------------------------ |\n| Claude Code | `.mcp.json`              |\n| Codex       | `.codex/config.toml`     |\n| OpenCode    | `opencode.json`          |\n\nEach projector walks the cloned repo for folders that contain `SKILL.md`. A\nnested pack (`skills/foo/SKILL.md`) is linked under the skill name `foo`. A\nflat clone with `SKILL.md` at the root uses the clone name. You do not write\n`ln -s` by hand.\n\nA concept a given CLI lacks (for example, `plugins` on Codex) **emits a\nwarning and is silently skipped** rather than throwing. The same applies to\n`agentSkill` on Claude Code: there is no reliable primitive to install a public\nskill by bare name, so the projector warns and skips it. Prefer `gitSkill` (or a\n`plugins` entry) when you need that skill on Claude Code. That keeps one\nportable definition usable across harnesses: you declare everything once, and\neach agent takes the parts it understands.\n\n> These MCP servers are third-party services you point the agent at. Bridging\n> your **own app's host tools** into the agent (a `chat()` server tool whose\n> `execute()` runs back on the host) is a different mechanism, see\n> [Tools](./tools).\n\n## `AGENTS.md` and per-harness symlinks\n\n`instructions` is a string written to `AGENTS.md` at the workspace root during\nbootstrap. Harness-specific counterparts (`CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`) are\ncreated as **symlinks** to it; if the sandbox process layer cannot symlink, they\nare written as copies instead. Either way the instruction content is read\nnatively by every supported CLI without extra config.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo' }),\n  instructions: 'Always run `pnpm test` before proposing a change.',\n})\n```\n\n> Use `instructions` for guidance you want the agent to always follow. To\n> constrain what it is *allowed* to do, which commands and capabilities are\n> allowed, asked about, or denied, reach for [Policy](./policy) instead.\n"}
